    "title": "\"Exceptional drought\" hits Orange County - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Donate ,\n7 hours ago 2026 is North Carolina’s driest year since 1895. Possibly longer, as federal rainfall records don’t go back any further. The current drought is almost a year old, and with every month, it has gotten worse. Orange County, including Carrboro, is currently in a state of “exceptional drought,” the maximum level in the U.S. Drought Monitor’s classification system. Ending that would require a foot of rain within a month, and there’s no sign of that happening yet. Read full article",
